{"availability":"available","full":"ajaycyril/cloud-video-analyzer","name":"cloud-video-analyzer","description":"Edge-to-cloud physical AI video analytics demo with browser object detection, stateful evidence gating, and Gemini/OpenAI vision reasoning.","category":"Developer tools","language":"TypeScript","stars":0,"forks":0,"created":"2026-06-15T09:07:33Z","updated":"2026-06-22T03:47:00Z","branch":"main","homepage":"https://cloud-video-analyzer.vercel.app","topics":["computer-vision","edge-ai","gemini-api","mediapipe","multimodal-ai","nextjs","openai","physical-ai","pwa","roboflow","vercel","video-analytics"],"demo":"https://cloud-video-analyzer.vercel.app/","color":"#302e55","ink":"#dbd2ff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-08T18:23:37.321Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-08T18:23:37.321Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-08T18:23:37.321Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-08T18:23:37.321Z","stars":0,"forks":0}],"technologies":["Next.js"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Mobile-first edge-to-cloud video analytics platform for physical AI demos.","Cloud Video Analyzer shows how general-purpose multimodal AI can turn cameras into programmable analytics systems. A user can point a phone camera at a scene, upload a clip, or select a demo video, type the analytics they need in plain language, and receive structured alerts, scene evidence, recommended actions, latency, and estimated cloud cost.","The core architecture is intentionally hybrid: the browser acts as the edge device. It performs live object detection, motion analysis, scene-quality checks, evidence buffering, and stateful edge gating. Only qualified evidence frames are sent to Gemini/OpenAI/NVIDIA for higher-level reasoning. The full video is not uploaded by default."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/ajaycyril/cloud-video-analyzer/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"7d71d8738160d359f980d0c5b8fdf64106e85dfd7255b1dcc9a038a53f844dea","extractedAt":"2026-10-08T18:23:37.481Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-